During each planning interval, PAC-NMPC optimizes and returns policy hyperparameters, $ oldsymbol{
u}^*$, a PAC bound on the expected cost, $\mathcal{J}^+_\alpha( oldsymbol{
u}^*)$, and a PAC bound on the probability of constraint violation, $\mathcal{C}^+_\alpha( oldsymbol{
u}^*)$. These bounds serve as performance and safety guarantees for the policy; the probability of violating the obstacle constraint or worsening the learned value function, given the current LiDAR measurement, will be less than $\mathcal{C}^+_\alpha( oldsymbol{
u})$ with a probability of $1-\delta$ (eq. III-A).
